 "literal": "Swaying bamboo resembling of-beauty bamboo-like-shoulders / great beautiful eyes-she-who-has resided town-indeed / long distance difficult path is-that-indeed, O heart! / moisture received proper-time fresh field-in / single plow plowman like / great-distress attained-indeed, do I suffer, I-indeed!",
 "translation": "The town where she lives—she of the beautiful, wide eyes and shoulders as lovely as swaying bamboo—is far away, across a difficult path, O my heart! Yet, like a farmer with a single plow in a fresh field that has just received rain, you are in great haste and anxiety. How I suffer!",
 "modern": "அசையும் மூங்கிலைப் போன்ற அழகுடைய பருத்த தோள்களையும், பெரிய அழகிய கண்களையும் உடைய என் தலைவி வாழும் ஊரோ, மிகத் தொலைவில் உள்ள அரிய வழியைக் கடந்து செல்ல வேண்டிய இடத்தில் இருக்கிறது, நெஞ்சே! மழை பெய்து ஈரம் பட்டு உழுவதற்கு ஏற்ற பக்குவமடைந்த புதிய புனத்தில், ஒரே ஒரு ஏரை மட்டும் உடைய உழவன் படும் பதற்றத்தைப் போல, நீ பெரும் பதற்றத்தை அடைந்துள்ளாய். நானோ வருந்துகிறேன்!",
 "explanation": "In this poem of the wasteland (pālai) landscape, the hero speaks to his own heart while journeying away from his beloved. He laments that the town where his beautiful beloved resides is far away, separated by a long and difficult path. Yet, his heart is filled with intense haste and anxiety to return to her. He compares this inner turmoil to a farmer who has only a single plow to till a large, fresh field that has just received rain. Since the moisture in the soil will dry up quickly, the farmer is in extreme distress and hurry to complete the work with his limited means. This vivid agricultural metaphor perfectly captures the hero's feeling of urgency and helplessness in his separation.",
